# Product-molecularity fixture: one complex A.B.C. The rule deletes A-B and
# binds A to a C, claiming two products, A.C and B. The only C is the one bonded
# to B, which a bimolecular rule may match only with
# block_same_complex_binding=False; the bond the rule adds then joins A back to B
# through C, so the products do not separate and the rule must not fire (Bfree
# stays 0). With block_same_complex_binding=True there is no second complex.
begin model
begin parameters
  k 1
end parameters
begin molecule types
  A(b)
  B(a,c)
  C(b,x)
end molecule types
begin seed species
  A(b!1).B(a!1,c!2).C(b!2,x) 1
end seed species
begin observables
  Molecules Bfree B(a)
end observables
begin reaction rules
  A(b!1).B(a!1) + C(x) -> A(b!2).C(x!2) + B(a) k
end reaction rules
end model
writeXML()
